    "created_at": "2015-09-09T15:43:14Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-09-09T15:43:14Z",
    "body": "I believe this is the same thing. Here is the chromium bug tracking our effort to match the spec: https://code.google.com/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=517140\n\nThis was my main argument for keeping the current order: \n\n```\n I prefer option 2 mainly because the current order has the advantage that \n when 'popstate' is dispatched the application is guaranteed that the user-agent\n is done with restoring the state, and current values are reliable.\n```\n\nI still don't see a good solution around this issue. \n\nAlso if we change the spec order, what is expected behavior in cases where the popstate event handler sets the scroll position? I think user-agent should not override the script action by restoring the scroll position.\n\nFYI, I tested Edge and it still behaves according to the spec order.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
